WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.200
This is SPECTRA, a computer vision studio that runs entirely in your browser.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.818
Objects tracks each box with an ID.

00:00:07.918 --> 00:00:11.453
The new Library lists every class the detector can name.

00:00:12.248 --> 00:00:14.994
Hide one, and its boxes leave the stage.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.723
Finer names adds a second model's name beside each label, with its own score.

00:00:21.873 --> 00:00:25.238
Its classes have no person, so person stays hidden.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.781
Then a quick pass through the other modes, with Aura on.

00:00:28.931 --> 00:00:31.314
Each take skips its model's load time.

00:00:37.351 --> 00:00:41.740
The Ruler now measures a room, here a synthetic floor with known sizes.

00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:47.273
The reference is 1.2 by 0.9 metres.

00:00:51.047 --> 00:00:54.390
The taped outline is 3.84 square metres.

00:00:56.508 --> 00:01:01.601
SPECTRA reads 3.8, plus or minus 0.3 square metres.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:05.705
The bar is about nine percent and covers tap placement only.

00:01:05.805 --> 00:01:10.279
The top-down view redraws the floor to scale, and Save plan exports it.

00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:13.751
Presence measures head direction, hand movement and sway.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:17.458
Each has an error, and it says not seen when it cannot see.

00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:25.028
In the Lab, the stability meter shows raw jitter beside smoothed.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:28.419
The same studio fits a phone screen.

00:01:29.942 --> 00:01:31.515
Nothing is uploaded.

00:01:31.615 --> 00:01:33.251
The link is on screen.
